Two Seconds Short (差两秒) — Archive Light Table (Lemo-Opuscar) · LemoLab × Claude Opus 5.5
An unofficial film about a real event (the Wright brothers' flights of 17 December 1903) made only from
public-domain archive scans. No AI-generated images, no stock footage. The light table, glass, dust, loupe,
marks, readouts and camera are drawn in code (film.js). Sources accessed 2026-10-16; catalogue records in sources/.

ARCHIVE (Library of Congress; public domain, published before 1929; the Library lists no known restrictions on the
Wright Brothers Negatives)
- First flight, 120 feet in 12 seconds, 10:35 a.m.; Kitty Hawk, North Carolina. 1903 Dec. 17. Glass negative.
  Prints & Photographs Division, LC-DIG-ppprs-00626, https://hdl.loc.gov/loc.pnp/ppprs.00626
  File: https://tile.loc.gov/storage-services/master/pnp/ppprs/00600/00626u.tif
- Distant view of the Wright airplane just after landing … the fourth and final [flight] of December 17, 1903.
  Glass negative. LC-DIG-ppprs-00629, https://hdl.loc.gov/loc.pnp/ppprs.00629
  File: https://tile.loc.gov/storage-services/master/pnp/ppprs/00600/00629u.tif
- Wilbur in prone position in damaged machine … unsuccessful trial of December 14, 1903. Glass negative.
  LC-DIG-ppprs-00610, https://hdl.loc.gov/loc.pnp/ppprs.00610
  File: https://tile.loc.gov/storage-services/master/pnp/ppprs/00600/00610u.tif
- Newspaper notice of Wright Bros. 1st flight: Dayton Herald, Dec. 18, 1903. LC-USZ62-70686,
  https://hdl.loc.gov/loc.pnp/cph.3b18080
  File: https://tile.loc.gov/storage-services/master/pnp/cph/3b10000/3b18000/3b18000/3b18080u.tif
- Telegram from Orville Wright in Kitty Hawk, N.C., to his father announcing four successful flights, 1903 Dec. 17.
  Wilbur and Orville Wright Papers, Manuscript Division (P&P copy LC-USZ62-65459, https://hdl.loc.gov/loc.pnp/cph.3b12982).
  Colour scan from https://www.loc.gov/resource/mcc.061/ via Wikimedia Commons, public domain:
  https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Telegram_Orville_Wright_17_dec_1903.jpg
- Modifications: inversion to a negative for the light table, emulsion masks, levels, the Flyer and Wilbur cut into
  layers with the background filled (tools/prep.py), the telegram's scan mat trimmed.

